            <ArticleTitle>Ross River Virus Seroprevalence, French Polynesia, 2014-2015.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>1751-1753</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.3201/eid2310.170583</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Ross River virus (RRV), spread by Aedes and Culex mosquitoes, is the most commonly transmitted arbovirus in Australia. A serosurvey of blood donors in French Polynesia during 2011-2013 suggested that RRV circulated without being detected. We report RRV circulation in French Polynesia based on further screening of blood samples collected during 2014-2015.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
